WEBVTT

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:10.630
Th-Thank you.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.970
Welcome, friends.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:22.640
I am Daniel Klausner,
the lord overseeing this region.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.610
I'm Sei Takanashi.
Thank you for hosting us.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.820
I'm Albert Hawke, Commander
of the Third Order of Knights.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:30.860
We are honored to serve you.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.580
I'm exhausted.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.540
Would you like to change out of your robe?

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:16.010
I've got dinner with Lord Klausner
later tonight, don't I?

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:18.220
Yes, but you have some time until then,

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:21.550
if you'd like to change into
something more comfortable.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:22.760
Then I'm definitely changing!

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:29.310
Wearing this robe makes
my shoulders get all achy.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:34.070
If your robe is causing you discomfort,
then might I suggest a formal dress?

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:37.030
Nope, the robe is totally fine!

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:38.450
Very well.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:47.330
This is delicious!

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:51.750
I believe it's infused with herbs
we rarely see in the capital.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.290
This region <i>is </i>known
for its herb cultivation.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:03:01.300
I bet the Alchemist's Holy Land is
gonna seem like heaven for you, Sei.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.890
What do you mean?

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:06.220
There are alchemist families
there that go back generations,

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:08.980
and they all have their
own secret recipes.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:13.150
Who knows, you might find a way to make
potions stronger than high-grade ones.

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:17.280
Secret potion recipes...

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.040
I hope it's to your liking.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.880
It's fantastic! Is this a local recipe?

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:34.920
No, actually.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:38.670
We heard rumors that using herbs in
cooking had become popular at the palace,

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:41.050
and merely adopted the practice.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.630
I see.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:46.560
All right, then. That makes this
one of <i>my </i>recipes, technically.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.560
They're using a much more complex
combination of herbs than I did, though.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.480
Klausner's Domain just keeps
impressing me more and more!

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:59.280
What types of herbs do you cultivate here?

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.360
I spotted a few I was unfamiliar with
as we traveled into your domain.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:09.290
We take great pride in being the number
one producer of herbs in the kingdom.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:13.210
I hear you enjoy the crafting
of potions, Lady Sei.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:17.960
Yes. I make plenty for the Palace's
Medicinal Flora Research Institute.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:22.420
Is that so? Then you must be
quite the competent alchemist.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:25.510
Oh, I wouldn't say I'm <i>that </i>good...

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:29.180
We have our own practitioners
here in the castle.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:32.560
Including one many call
the best in the entire domain.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:35.230
The <i>best</i>, you say?

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:40.110
If you'd like, I can
arrange an introduction.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.280
I'd love that, thank you!

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:55.540
I got so distracted by all that
talk of herbs and alchemy

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:58.590
that I forgot to ask
about monster attacks.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:09.470
Don't worry. I asked the palace guard
about that before we went to dinner.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:10.310
Huh?

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:14.180
I figured you would be exhausted
from our long journey.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.230
Thank you.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:18.190
We'll start our expeditions
tomorrow, then?

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:21.860
Oh, no. We'll need to spend
a few days scouting out the area.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:24.190
You can spend that time
relaxing here in the castle.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.900
All right.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:29.870
Then maybe I'll see if I can
meet that master alchemist.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:33.500
I also want to make some potions
while I can, then ask about herbs...

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:36.540
Oh, right, there's something
important I've forgotten.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.130
What is it?

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:41.130
You look stunning in that robe.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:42.670
Huh?

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:44.760
Your beauty nearly took my breath away.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:50.350
Th-Thank you very much!

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:56.770
Y-You also look, uh, very...

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:57.770
Very?

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:01.270
N-Never mind!

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.540
Corinna.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:19.000
Well, if it isn't milord Klausner.
How can I help you?

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:23.210
This is the Saint, Lady Sei,
who has just arrived from the capital.

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:25.460
Hello, I'm Sei Takanashi.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:27.550
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:32.550
My name is Corinna, and I'm one
of the castle's alchemists.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:37.770
Lady Sei has a great interest
in medicinal herbs.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:40.400
She'd like to learn a few things
from you, if that's all right.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.400
If you wouldn't mind!

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:47.280
Not at all. I was just about to start
making today's batch of potions.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.610
How about we chat while I get that done?

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:53.870
I'd love that, actually!
Would you mind if I helped you with that?

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:57.080
Yes! A chance to learn
from a master alchemist!

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:59.040
Of course. This way, dear.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:00.790
Thank you, ma'am!

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:07.630
I leave her in your
capable hands, Corinna.

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:09.260
Of course, milord.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:23.360
All right, next!

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:25.070
N-Now hold on a moment.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:27.360
You can still make <i>more</i>?

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:29.650
I usually make much more than this.

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:30.650
What?!

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:34.490
U-Uh...

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:37.490
When I heard the Saint
liked making potions,

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:41.080
I thought it would be
no more than a hobby.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.790
But here you are, outdoin' me
in my own workshop!

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:46.750
Th-Thank you, ma'am.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:51.800
I can see we'll be able to have <i>much </i>more
interesting conversations, Lady Sei.

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:57.720
Actually, could you please
stop calling me "Lady" Sei?

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:01.850
You sure? Then just Sei is fine?

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:02.940
Yes, please!

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:04.980
Right then, Sei, I--

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:05.980
Yo!

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.190
Wow.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:11.610
His arms are <i>huge</i>.

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:17.660
Why do you always have to make such
a ruckus? Can't you pipe down for once?

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.660
Finally got yourself another
apprentice, Granny?

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:25.710
Don't be silly. She's not my apprentice.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:28.550
Never mind that. What do you want?

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:32.010
Uh, I'm here for those potions we ordered.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:33.340
What?!

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:37.850
You put in that order last night!
You really thought we'd be done by now?

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.270
You do realize these
things take time, yes?

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:43.810
W-Well, yeah, I know that,

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:45.980
but they just told us to sortie
all of the sudden, so...

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:48.440
He reminds me of a puppy.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:51.740
Well, they're ready.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:56.030
Knew we could count on ya, Granny!

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:57.950
Thank Sei, not me.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:59.280
Who's Sei?

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:05.040
Sei here made all of these potions.
I can vouch for their quality.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.420
Hello, I'm Sei.

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:09.750
I'm Leonhardt, captain of the mercenary
company stationed in the castle!

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:12.570
It's nice to meet--

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:15.630
Thanks for helpin' out! I owe ya one!

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:17.470
S-Sure.

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:20.640
Leo! She's <i>not </i>one of your mercenaries!

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:21.720
Sorry!

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:27.810
I swear, if you'd take a moment
to <i>think </i>every now and then...

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:30.360
I know, sorry, Granny...

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:32.900
He really is like a big, clumsy dog.

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:44.960
I was able to attain a measurement
of the Saint's magic power today.

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:46.330
And?

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:49.920
She is most certainly our Saint.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:54.170
Then Lady Sei will be able
to bless our fields?

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:57.760
I can't be sure of
that yet, unfortunately.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:01.890
But I did learn something very promising.

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:07.480
While she was present at the Institute,
she was witnessed casting golden magic.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:10.770
She was? The same magic
described in that diary?

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:12.320
I believe so.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:16.490
This Saint has a great interest
in the crafting of potions.

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:18.740
If we were to show her
the alchemist's diary,

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:21.870
she may discover how to
perform the blessing herself.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:30.960
She must.
The Saint is our last and only hope.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:45.890
Do you remember what these
herbs are used for, Sei?

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:50.600
When combined with other herbs, they
boost the healing potential of potions,

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:55.150
so, by adding them to other recipes,
you can use less herbs altogether.

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:56.690
Do I have that right?

00:10:56.690 --> 00:11:02.070
That you do. You've memorized
most of my house's recipes, then.

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:03.700
Thank you so much for teaching me.

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:08.500
I'm so grateful I got the chance
to come here and learn from you!

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:13.090
Please, you've taught me
plenty of things, too.

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:17.800
For example, I had no idea this wheat
provided an additional health boost.

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:23.640
In my world, they call it "spelt wheat,"
and it's packed with nutrients.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:28.730
No matter how old I get,
there's always something new to learn.

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:34.690
I wonder what would happen if
we mixed this wheat into a potion...

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:38.740
Could it make a potion that's more
effective than high-grade potions?

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:42.070
Is that what you want to make, now?

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:45.910
Yes. I've done plenty of research,
but I can't seem to find any recipes...

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.660
They existed, way long ago.

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.330
Really?!

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.710
Yes, but not anymore.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:11:59.800
Come.

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:26.410
Sei.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:30.410
What's that?

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:33.080
A diary, and one of our
most precious tomes.

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:38.960
It was written by the Great Alchemist,

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.970
the mother of Klausner's
alchemic know-how.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:44.680
The Great Alchemist?

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:46.180
Read it.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:47.760
Are you sure it's all right?

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:48.760
Yes.

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:52.680
You're the one person
who <i>should </i>read it, Sei.

00:12:54.730 --> 00:12:57.310
Put it back in the safe when you're done.

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:14.910
I love the people of Klausner's Domain.

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:17.780
I love this land they call home.

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:20.370
I've never been to the capital,

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:23.460
but I'm sure Klausner's
Domain would outshine it.

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:30.130
But this year's drought is horrific.

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:35.300
Crops are dying, and our precious
herbs have all wasted away.

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:39.850
And it's not just the herbs.
Our wheat, our crops, everything.

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:46.050
This famine has lasted over a month, now.
Everyone is slowly starving.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:51.310
If only there were <i>something</i>
I could do to help!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:57.480
A horrible disease spreads
amongst the people,

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:02.110
and my darling younger brother,
Curt, is bedridden with it.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:06.280
I can barely stand to see how gaunt his
chubby, rosy cheeks have now become.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:11.030
I can't allow this famine to continue.

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:13.330
I must change our fate for the better.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:20.040
My research has taught me how
to craft new forms of medicine.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:25.830
I had hoped they could cure Curt,
but I can't cultivate the needed herbs.

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:30.960
If I can't grow them, then he won't be
cured, no matter how often he's Healed.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:33.670
Is there any way to restore
vitality to our land?

00:14:37.130 --> 00:14:42.220
Today, Curt sang me a beautiful song.

00:14:42.220 --> 00:14:47.230
He suffers so greatly, yet he still
finds the strength for kindness.

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:49.810
What am I to do to save you?

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:51.850
I love you, my sweet Curt.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:54.900
Please, don't die.

00:14:56.030 --> 00:14:59.400
Curt, Curt, Curt...

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:06.900
A brilliant gold flowed across the fields.

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:13.240
I've been so busy, I barely had
time to write in this diary.

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:17.330
The famine came to an end, and our
crops began to grow once more,

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:22.170
and Curt's cheeks grew
plump and rosy again.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:24.630
My darling, beloved Curt.

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:30.470
I dub this magic a blessing,

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:32.930
as it was Curt who gifted it to me.

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:44.540
Was the Great Alchemist a Saint?

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:54.220
Golden magic, blessings...

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.260
But how was she able to cast it?

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:57.930
Do we have any more potions?!

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:59.390
We're all out!

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.020
Do we have any mages
who can Heal the wounded?!

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.350
No, of course not!

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:03.400
What's going on?

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.880
Is everything all right?!

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:21.180
Hey, it's you.

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:25.610
Just ran into some rare monsters near
the forest. Got our asses handed to us.

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:27.320
And now you're all injured?

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:29.820
Nah, we're doin' just fine.

00:16:29.820 --> 00:16:32.610
Those potions you made
for us saved our skin.

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:34.700
Whoa, <i>you </i>made those potions?

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:37.910
They were so damn effective!

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:41.710
So, uh, would you like me
to get you some more?

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:44.000
I hear we're completely out of potions.

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:47.130
Don't worry, though, a little rest
and we'll be right as rain.

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:50.380
Sure, but a few of you
are still gravely wounded.

00:16:56.180 --> 00:17:00.020
Uh, if you'd like, I can Heal you.

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:02.230
Thanks, but we're outta potions.

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:06.230
No, not with potions, with, uh, magic.

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:10.150
Wait, I thought you were an alchemist.

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:11.780
Well, uh...

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:15.610
Yep, I'm an alchemist!

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:19.740
Let me heal you!

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:20.870
A-All right.

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:25.000
<i>Heal</i>.

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:36.390
I've never seen someone cast Heal before.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:38.050
Me neither.

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:42.220
You say you're an alchemist, but you're
<i>also </i>damn good at healing magic!

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:45.190
Th-Thanks?

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:46.980
Wish we could recruit you into our squad.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:53.240
If you can Heal people, the Knights
might call for your help, too.

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:58.410
They ran into a nasty group
of monsters out there.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:59.990
Huh?

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:04.750
W-Wait, you mean the Knights
that came here from the capital?

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:06.290
Yeah, of course.

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:11.000
They went out to scout the area, but got
pinned down by a big horde of 'em.

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:12.750
Wait...

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:15.010
We'll need to spend a few days
scouting out the area.

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:24.060
N-No...

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:29.310
<i>Area heal</i>!

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:43.910
Wh-What the hell was <i>that</i>?

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:53.050
Please, please!

00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:58.680
Volf!

00:18:58.680 --> 00:18:59.680
Sei!

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:01.470
Are you all right?!

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:06.060
We all made it back alive, thankfully,
though plenty came back wounded.

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:07.180
Let me help!

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:15.400
Sei!

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:17.740
Commander! Commander!

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:21.660
Sei?

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:30.710
No.

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:33.630
No, you can't!

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:38.510
Please, <i>please</i>!

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:47.350
Commander!

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:50.350
Sei?

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:03.910
What?

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:14.290
Wait... Huh?

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:25.470
Thank you for your help.
I can't express how grateful we are.

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:29.430
P-Please, you flatter me.
I'm sorry to cause such a fuss.

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:32.690
I totally thought you'd
been horribly hurt.

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:38.190
I feel terrible for causing
you such distress.

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:40.940
Though I do somewhat like the thought
of you worrying for my health.

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:48.080
Still, how was it that you were
able to use that magic just then?

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:50.540
R-Right?! I want to know that, too!

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:55.460
First the Western Forest, now here.

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:57.840
Perhaps it was because you
believed someone was in danger?

00:20:57.840 --> 00:20:59.920
No, I don't think so...

00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:02.720
The first time it happened,
no one was in any danger at all.

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:08.720
I was just...

00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:20.400
Sei?

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:21.400
Yeah?!

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.110
Are you all right? Your face has gone--

00:21:23.110 --> 00:21:24.990
I'm completely all right, really!

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:26.490
You don't <i>look </i>all right...

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.790
P-Please don't look at me right now!

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:31.830
Sei?

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:39.710
H-How am I supposed to tell him
<i>that </i>embarrassing fact?!

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:50.310
I couldn't!

00:21:56.810 --> 00:21:59.730
I know now...

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:02.650
...that the Saint's power

00:22:02.010 --> 00:22:05.010
Diary

00:22:02.650 --> 00:22:04.490
is the power of love itself.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
Next Time

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
Dilemma
